For quick reference let us compile a table of the constructions looked at so far. A `X' indicates that the category is closed under the respective construction, a `+' says that, in addition, the construction plays the expected categorical role as a product, exponential or coproduct, respectively. Observe that for the constructions considered in this section it makes no difference if we restrict the size of a (minimal) basis.

\begin{center}
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{0.55em}
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.15}
\begin{tabular}{lccccccc}
\hline
Construction & $\mathbf{DCPO}$ & $\mathbf{DCPO}_{\bot}$ & $\mathbf{DCPO}_{\bot!}$ & $\mathbf{CONT}$ & $\mathbf{ALG}$ & $\mathbf{CONT}_{\bot}$/$\mathbf{ALG}_{\bot}$ & $\mathbf{CONT}_{\bot!}$/$\mathbf{ALG}_{\bot!}$\\
\hline
$D\times E$ & $+$ & $+$ & $+$ & $+$ & $+$ & $+$ & $+$\\
$[D\to E]$ & $+$ & $+$ & $X$ &  &  &  & \\
$D\cup E$ & $+$ &  &  & $+$ &  &  & \\
$D\otimes E$ &  & $X$ & $X$ &  &  & $X$ & $X$\\
$[D\xrightarrow{\bot!}E]$ &  & $X$ & $+$ &  &  &  & \\
$D\oplus E$ &  & $X$ & $+$ &  &  & $X$ & $+$\\
$D_{\bot}$ & $X$ & $X$ & $X$ & $X$ & $X$ & $X$ & $X$\\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

